{"authored" [{"question" "q-9255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(3,2),(14,6),$ and $(9,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\n- $(3,2)$\n- $(1,1)$\n- $(5,1)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991959/state.json" "file_sha256" "422df6a64af4c3eeea14a66586241df28f9811f88637adb871c544dc0f6f079b" "basis" 1036 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991959/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2-0}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-1,1),(2,3),(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991959/state.json" "file_sha256" "422df6a64af4c3eeea14a66586241df28f9811f88637adb871c544dc0f6f079b" "basis" 1036 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991959/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991959/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5237f93d747e0b2a6a8e489732189fd49a995c27680926bd5ea8541bd7c2baa3" "basis" 1036 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991959/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991959/state.json" "file_sha256" "422df6a64af4c3eeea14a66586241df28f9811f88637adb871c544dc0f6f079b" "basis" 1036 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991959/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991959/state.json" "file_sha256" "422df6a64af4c3eeea14a66586241df28f9811f88637adb871c544dc0f6f079b" "basis" 1036 "