stion-capture/14014369/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bc3778e42f0a612e0dabe1b452dd159240796d5ee616448cf95b740a84d8107" "basis" 1192 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bc3778e42f0a612e0dabe1b452dd159240796d5ee616448cf95b740a84d8107" "basis" 1192 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-9263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bc3778e42f0a612e0dabe1b452dd159240796d5ee616448cf95b740a84d8107" "basis" 1192 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bc3778e42f0a612e0dabe1b452dd159240796d5ee616448cf95b740a84d8107" "basis" 1192 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6-5}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/state.json" "file_sha256" "2bc3778e42f0a612e0dabe1b452dd159240796d5ee616448cf95b740a84d8107" "basis" 1192 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dd45c604be785a4cb8d791de7709ff54f6180db9c87ae17f485093ed2549b51a" "basis" 1192 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014369/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85077" "fi